## 6. The `handleInputRestore` Effect (Full Code)

**File:** `C:\Users\zemuro\Antigravity\kimi_extension_mod\webview-ui\src\components\inputarea\InputArea.tsx`, lines 86–105

```typescript
  // Restore pending input
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!pendingInput || isStreaming) {
      return;
    }

    // 只在输入框为空时恢复
    if (inputDraft.trim()) {
      return;
    }

    const textContent = Content.getText(pendingInput.content);
    if (textContent) {
      setInputDraft(textContent);
      setTimeout(() => {
        textareaRef.current?.focus();
        adjustHeight();
      }, 0);
    }
  }, [pendingInput, isStreaming]);
```

There is **no named function** called `handleInputRestore` anywhere in the codebase. The above `useEffect` is the only mechanism that restores previously-sent input into the textarea. It fires when:
- `pendingInput` becomes non-null (e.g., after a preflight error sets `pendingInput`)
- `isStreaming` becomes false (so the stream is done and the input can be restored)
- The textarea is currently empty (won't overwrite user's new draft)
